// Get the SDL joystick layer bindings for a gamepad.
//
// Parameters:
//   - gamepad: a gamepad.
//   - count: a pointer filled in with the number of bindings returned.
//
// Returns: a NULL terminated array of pointers to bindings or NULL on failure; call GetError() for more information. This is a single allocation that should be freed with Free() when it is no longer needed.
//
// Thread safety: It is safe to call this function from any thread.
//
// Since: SDL 3.2.0.
//
// The SDL allocation is copied into the returned slice and released. A nil result means SDL reported failure (see GetError); a non-nil empty slice means success with no items.
